--- a/docs/design/cubic-fp-collision.md
+++ b/docs/design/cubic-fp-collision.md
@@ -91,6 +91,20 @@ The raw analytical function remains available as a diagnostic control. The
 bounded function is the candidate for the next homogeneous comparison, not yet
 a production solver choice.
 
+The Stage-3 continuous bounded-source experiment passed all 36 focused Julia
+tests but was too stiff from its first macro step: the source norm was
+`1.38e5`, and explicit Euler requested `h/dt < 2^-24`. FPCode does not integrate
+this bounded model as an Euler source; it uses an exact-OU finite-step map.
+
+`fp_collision_step35_bounded` therefore applies that same map to the CHyQMOM
+nodes. The stochastic increment is integrated analytically: each mapped node
+becomes an isotropic Gaussian with the FPCode noise variance, and its raw
+moments through degree four are accumulated exactly. A final isotropic affine
+map is the deterministic moment counterpart of the homogeneous particle
+validator's recenter/rescale. This is the appropriate algorithm-to-algorithm
+comparison; the continuous bounded source remains available only as a recorded
+negative result.
+
 ## Acceptance gates before solver wiring
 
 1. Maxwellian stationarity in the Ornstein--Uhlenbeck limit (`Pr=1`).
